{
  "_id": "CpizBXkbF6fIm86R",
  "name": "Power Word Pain",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/magic/unholy/beams-impact-pink.webp",
  "folder": "yF36NiycTV8uw4AQ",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You speak a word of power that sends waves of intense pain through a creature you can see within range. If it has 100 Hit Points or fewer, it takes 6d8 Force damage and has the &amp;Reference[charmed apply=false]{Charmed} condition for the duration; otherwise, it takes 6d8 Force damage only.</p><p>While Charmed, the target’s Speed can be no more than 10 feet, and it has Disadvantage on D20 Tests other than Constitution saving throws. In addition, when it tries to cast a spell, it must first succeed on a Constitution saving throw or the spell dissipates with no effect, wasting the action, Bonus Action, or Reaction used to cast it; if the spell was cast with a spell slot, the slot isn’t expended.</p><p>At the end of each of its turns, the Charmed target makes a Constitution saving throw, ending the spell on itself on a success.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-ooHXBurpsHLgMqRi\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Apply the effect only to a target with 100 Hit Points or fewer; it limits the walking Speed and gives the Disadvantage on ability checks and saving throws (attack rolls by hand).</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
